# Cross-Session Facts — {{USER}}

Loaded into every session by `scripts/hooks/session-start.sh`.

**Keep this under 80 lines.** It costs context on every single session, so only
durable, reusable facts belong here. Anything topical belongs in the wiki
instead, where `wiki-recall.sh` fetches it on demand when a prompt matches.

Updated when a correction reveals a reusable fact — see
`scripts/hooks/correction-detection.sh`.

Good entries look like:

- A convention that is not discoverable from the code (why a thing is done a
  particular way, when the code only shows that it is).
- A toolchain detail an agent would otherwise rediscover each session (where the
  venv lives, which test runner, a required env var).
- A trap that already cost someone time, stated as the rule that avoids it.

Bad entries:

- Anything the repo already records — file layout, git history, CLAUDE.md.
- Anything true only this week. Put it in a handoff.
- Long explanations. One or two lines each; link to a wiki article for depth.

